WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:11.813
"Look, Dad!" Lila said, waving a flyer.

2
00:00:11.814 --> 00:00:17.482
"The amusement park is having a roller coaster design contest.

3
00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:23.339
First prize is two tickets for the first ride on the new coaster!"

4
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.360
Dad leaned back and pretended he was riding a roller coaster.

5
00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:31.239
"I love when I'm pushed back in the seat."

6
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.212
"It only feels like you're being pushed back.

7
00:00:35.213 --> 00:00:38.746
The seat is really pushing you forward."

8
00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:44.111
Dad laughed. "You sure know your stuff!"

9
00:00:44.112 --> 00:00:47.147
Lila started drawing ideas.

10
00:00:47.148 --> 00:00:49.926
First she drew a lift hill.

11
00:00:49.927 --> 00:00:54.652
She knew that roller coasters didn't have motors.

12
00:00:54.653 --> 00:01:01.383
The cars gained speed as gravity pulled them down from the top of the lift hill.

13
00:01:01.384 --> 00:01:05.952
This momentum would carry the cars through the rest of the roller coaster.

14
00:01:05.953 --> 00:01:09.891
"My hill looks too short," Lila thought.

15
00:01:09.892 --> 00:01:15.520
"The cars won't have enough momentum to go through loops or over hills."

16
00:01:15.521 --> 00:01:17.969
She made the hill a bit taller.

17
00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:22.345
If she made it too tall, the cars would gain too much speed.

18
00:01:22.346 --> 00:01:25.397
Then the ride would be uncomfortable or dangerous.

19
00:01:25.398 --> 00:01:32.083
After the lift hill, Lila added loops, hills, and curves.

20
00:01:32.084 --> 00:01:34.226
"Yes!" Lila declared.

21
00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:38.412
She was almost ready to build a model!

22
00:01:38.413 --> 00:01:43.555
As Dad drove to the park, Lila practiced explaining her model.

23
00:01:43.556 --> 00:01:50.836
"Gravity pulls you down at the top of the loop, but the momentum keeps pushing you forward."

24
00:01:50.837 --> 00:01:54.343
"That gives you the weightless feeling?" Dad asked.

25
00:01:54.344 --> 00:01:58.523
"Exactly."

26
00:01:58.524 --> 00:02:00.810
Dad parked.

27
00:02:00.811 --> 00:02:05.731
As Lila started to get out of the car, the box slipped from her hands.

28
00:02:05.732 --> 00:02:10.619
Lila gasped as her model crashed onto the pavement.

29
00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:16.334
"It's ruined! What am I going to do? Judging starts soon!"

30
00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:19.573
Dad helped her pick up the pieces.

31
00:02:19.574 --> 00:02:25.007
"It's not too bad. You'll think of something."

32
00:02:25.008 --> 00:02:29.142
In the waiting room, Lila examined the other contestants' designs.

33
00:02:29.143 --> 00:02:32.531
Some wouldn't work, but others were good.

34
00:02:32.532 --> 00:02:36.220
She stared at the pieces of her model in the box.

35
00:02:36.221 --> 00:02:38.774
"Hey!" she thought suddenly.

36
00:02:38.775 --> 00:02:45.041
"Maybe I can put the pieces together as I explain my model!"

37
00:02:45.042 --> 00:02:51.045
Soon it was Lila's turn. In the judging room, Lila put the lift hill on the table.

38
00:02:51.046 --> 00:02:55.092
"A cable pulls the cars to the top."

39
00:02:55.093 --> 00:02:58.906
Next she put the loop on the table.

40
00:02:58.907 --> 00:03:04.962
"From the lift hill, the cars should have enough speed to go through this loop."

41
00:03:04.963 --> 00:03:09.901
"Why isn't the loop round?" judge number one asked.

42
00:03:09.902 --> 00:03:14.577
"A round loop makes the cars go the same speed all around.

43
00:03:14.578 --> 00:03:22.189
This teardrop shape slows the speed on the sides of the loop to make the ride more comfortable."

44
00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.511
The judges nodded.

45
00:03:23.512 --> 00:03:26.747
Lila's plan was working!

46
00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:31.008
But as she took the last piece from the box, her heart sank.

47
00:03:31.009 --> 00:03:34.453
Part of the track was twisted upside down!

48
00:03:34.454 --> 00:03:38.892
"Interesting," judge number two said.

49
00:03:38.893 --> 00:03:42.789
"This isn't how I designed it," Lila admitted.

50
00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:47.512
"I dropped the model in the parking lot."

51
00:03:47.513 --> 00:03:53.112
"Do you think it would work on a real coaster?" judge number one asked.

52
00:03:53.113 --> 00:04:03.474
"Hmm. I think the momentum coming out of the loop would carry the cars through the twist."

53
00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:07.069
Lila sat nervously in the waiting room.

54
00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:10.628
"I couldn't answer the twist question."

55
00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:14.186
"I'm sure you did well," Dad assured her.

56
00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:18.946
Finally the judges called everyone back in.

57
00:04:18.947 --> 00:04:24.980
"The winner is Lila King!" judge number one announced.

58
00:04:24.981 --> 00:04:31.169
"For her good model and her great knowledge of roller coaster physics!"

59
00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:37.734
Judge number two shook Lila's hand and handed her the tickets.

60
00:04:37.735 --> 00:04:43.110
"My company has a summer camp for future engineers," he said.

61
00:04:43.111 --> 00:04:46.014
"You should think about attending."

62
00:04:46.015 --> 00:04:57.146
Lila grinned. "I'll definitely look into it—after I ride the new coaster!"
